# Cognito sign-in
#
# The portal signs in through the same Cognito Hosted UI the games app uses,
# with the same user pool and app client. That flow only needs two public
# values, both defaulted in src/auth/oauth.js to the deployed games app:
#
#   domain    reimondev.auth.us-east-2.amazoncognito.com
#   client    77ieg4fiv0dg7fo5g9uqb1n5rm
#
# So no configuration is required. The optional overrides below exist for
# pointing a build at a different app client.
#
# REACT_APP_AUTH_COGNITO_DOMAIN=reimondev.auth.us-east-2.amazoncognito.com
# REACT_APP_AUTH_USER_POOL_CLIENT_ID=77ieg4fiv0dg7fo5g9uqb1n5rm
#
# One Cognito console change is required: the app client must allow these
# callback URLs (it already has the games app's /games/oauth2/callback):
#
#   https://reimondev.com/login
#   http://localhost:3000/login
#
# Without that, Cognito answers with "redirect_mismatch" instead of signing in.
# No user pool ID is needed anywhere in this app.
#
# Fallback, if the console is out of reach: point the portal at the games
# app's already-allow-listed callback. Sign-in then finishes inside /games,
# which stores the session, and the portal picks it up on the next page view.
#
# REACT_APP_AUTH_REDIRECT_URI=https://reimondev.com/games/oauth2/callback
